# Sample requests. Visual Studio and Rider run this file as is. VS Code needs the REST Client extension.
# Start both apps first (see README.md).
#
# Change the policy number to act out a failure:
#   POL-100            everything works
#   POL-INACTIVE       the policy does not cover the claim
#   POL-FAIL-CASE      opening the case fails
#   POL-FAIL-ADJUSTER  assigning the adjuster fails
#   POL-FAIL-NOTIFY    the email fails
#   POL-FAIL-RELEASE   the adjuster step fails, then the reserve cannot be released

@api = http://localhost:5100
@stubs = http://localhost:5200

### Submit a claim. Use a new Idempotency-Key for each new attempt.
POST {{api}}/claims
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-1

{
  "policyNumber": "POL-100",
  "claimantEmail": "pat@example.com",
  "lossDate": "2026-01-15",
  "estimatedAmount": 2500.00
}

### See what is still open and the order of the calls.
GET {{stubs}}/debug/state
